<RootLayout
  metadata={{
    title: "Privacy Policy — Soulful Bhakti",
    description:
      "Privacy Policy for the Soulful Bhakti Android app, explaining what data is collected, why, how it is used and shared, how it is protected, and how to delete your account and data.",
    keywords:
      "Soulful Bhakti, privacy policy, privacy, data, account deletion, devotional music",
    author: "Soulful Bhakti",
  }}
>
  <section class="p-4 md:p-16">
    <h2 class="h2">Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p class="opacity-70">Effective date: 25 August 2026</p>

    <br />

    <div class="prose lg:prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-4xl">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Soulful Bhakti</strong>, an
        application published by <strong>FAMERELAY</strong> (together
        &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;), accesses,
        collects, uses, handles and shares information in connection with the
        Soulful Bhakti Android app and related services (&ldquo;the
        Service&rdquo;). It also explains your choices, including how to request
        deletion of your account and associated data.
      </p>
      <p>
        By using the Service, you agree to the collection, use and sharing of
        information as described in this policy. This policy is provided in
        accordance with the Google Play User Data policy and Google Play&rsquo;s
        requirements for developer privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Overview</h3>
      <p>
        Soulful Bhakti is a devotional music streaming app. The Service can be
        used without creating an account. Signing in with your Google account is
        optional and is required only to sync your playlists, like songs, track
        listening history, and to access paid (premium) content and
        subscriptions. The Service does <strong>not</strong> display third-party
        advertising, and we do <strong>not</strong> sell personal or sensitive
        user data.
      </p>

      <h3>2. Information We Access and Collect</h3>
      <p>
        We access and collect information only to provide, secure and improve the
        Service, consistent with what users reasonably expect from the Service.
        The information we handle falls into the categories below, which also
        appear in our Google Play Data safety declarations.
      </p>

      <h4>a. Information you provide</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Account information (Personal info):</strong> When you sign in
          with your Google account through our authentication provider
          (Clerk), we receive your name, email address, profile picture and a
          unique account identifier. You can use the Service without providing
          this information; this data is collected only when you choose to sign
          in.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>User-generated content (App activity):</strong> Playlists you
          create, songs you like, and your listening history. This content is
          stored in our backend database (Supabase) when you are signed in and
          remains on your device (local database) even when you are signed out.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h4>b. Information we collect automatically</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>App interactions (App activity):</strong> Analytics events
          about how you use the app, collected through Firebase Analytics (for
          example, which features you use).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Crash logs and diagnostics (App info and performance):</strong>
          Anonymous technical data about crashes and performance, collected
          through Firebase Crashlytics, so we can fix bugs and improve
          reliability.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Device or other IDs:</strong> A Firebase installation ID and a
          push-notification subscription ID (OneSignal). These are
          application-level identifiers that can be reset by the user. We do
          <strong>not</strong> collect or link persistent hardware device
          identifiers such as IMEI, IMSI or SIM serial numbers to personal or
          sensitive user data. The push subscription is created only if you opt
          in to push notifications; notification permission is requested only
          from a user-initiated action and never at launch.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Purchase history (Financial info):</strong> If you subscribe
          to premium or make an in-app purchase, payment and transaction details
          are processed by Google Play Billing (through our payment provider,
          Superwall). We do not collect or store your full payment card details;
          those are handled by Google. We never publicly disclose financial or
          payment information.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Affiliate attribution:</strong> If you install the app from an
          affiliate QR code or link, a short, non-identifying referral code
          (utm_source) is read from the Google Play Install Referrer so we can
          attribute the referral. This is attribution-only and is not used to
          change prices.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3. How We Use Information</h3>
      <p>
        We use the information we collect only for purposes that are reasonably
        expected from the Service and disclosed in this policy:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide, operate and maintain the Service (app functionality);</li>
        <li>
          Sync your playlists, liked songs and listening history across devices
          when you are signed in (account management);
        </li>
        <li>
          Manage subscriptions and grant access to premium content (app
          functionality, account management);
        </li>
        <li>
          Analyze how the Service is used and diagnose and fix bugs and crashes
          (analytics);
        </li>
        <li>
          Send you push notifications if you have opted in (developer
          communications);
        </li>
        <li>
          Prevent fraud, protect security and comply with legal obligations
          (fraud prevention, security and compliance).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4. Consent</h3>
      <p>
        Before we collect or access any data that requires consent, we request
        it through clear, in-app prompts that require an affirmative action by
        you. Where data is gated by an Android runtime permission, we request
        that permission at runtime, only when the relevant feature needs it, and
        only after you have seen the applicable disclosure. For example,
        permission to send push notifications is requested only after a
        user-initiated action and never at launch; you may grant or revoke it at
        any time in your device settings. You are never asked to provide
        information the Service does not need.
      </p>

      <h3>5. How We Share Information</h3>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> sell personal and sensitive user data. We
        share information only with service providers that process data on our
        behalf to help us operate the Service, and only to the extent necessary
        to provide it:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Play Services / Google Play Billing</strong> — sign-in
          and in-app purchase/subscription processing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Clerk</strong> — authentication (Google sign-in).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Supabase</strong> — cloud database and file storage for music,
          playlists and listening data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Firebase (Analytics and Crashlytics)</strong> — analytics and
          crash reporting.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>OneSignal</strong> — push notifications (only if you opt in).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Superwall</strong> — subscription paywalls and entitlements.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare R2</strong> — content delivery network used to
          stream audio.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These service providers are contractually obligated to use your
        information only on our behalf and for the purposes described in this
        policy. We may also disclose information where required by law, in
        response to a valid governmental request, or to protect the rights,
        property or safety of our users or the public.
      </p>

      <h3>6. Data Security</h3>
      <p>
        We take the protection of personal and sensitive user data seriously and
        handle it securely:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          All data transmitted between your device and our servers is encrypted
          in transit using modern cryptography (HTTPS/TLS).
        </li>
        <li>
          Access to personal and sensitive user data is limited to personnel and
          service providers who need it to provide and secure the Service.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not link persistent hardware device identifiers to personal and
          sensitive user data.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not collect data that is not necessary for the Service&rsquo;s
          functionality.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure, and we cannot
        guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h3>7. Data Retention and Deletion Policy</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Retention:</strong> We retain account-related data for as long as
        your account is active or as needed to provide the Service. Analytics and
        crash data are retained in a form that does not identify you. If we need
        to retain certain data for legitimate reasons such as security, fraud
        prevention or regulatory compliance, we retain only what is necessary and
        for the shortest period permitted by law.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Deletion on request:</strong> When you request account deletion,
        we permanently delete the data associated with your account (rather than
        merely deactivating or &ldquo;freezing&rdquo; it), except for any data we
        are required to retain by law, which we retain only for the legally
        required period and protect in accordance with this policy.
      </p>

      <h3>8. Account Deletion</h3>
      <p>
        You can request deletion of your Soulful Bhakti account and its
        associated data in either of the following ways:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Within the app:</strong> Use the account deletion option
          available in the app&rsquo;s profile/settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Outside the app (web):</strong> Submit a deletion request by
          emailing
          <a href="mailto:karthik@famerelay.com">karthik@famerelay.com</a> with
          the subject &ldquo;Account Deletion&rdquo;, using the email address
          associated with your account.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Upon receiving a deletion request, we delete all data associated with
        your account, as described in Section 7. If you are not signed in, you
        can delete the data stored on your device by uninstalling the app.
      </p>

      <h3>9. Children&rsquo;s Privacy</h3>
      <p>
        The Service is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a
        child under 13 has provided us with personal information, please contact
        us using the details below so we can delete it.
      </p>

      <h3>10. International Users</h3>
      <p>
        If you access the Service from the European Economic Area, the United
        Kingdom or Switzerland, we comply with applicable privacy and data
        protection laws, including the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)
        where it applies. You may have rights to access, correct, restrict,
        port or erase your personal data, and to object to its processing, by
        contacting us using the details below.
      </p>

      <h3>11. Your Choices and Rights</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Push notifications:</strong> You can grant or revoke
          notification permission at any time in your device settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sign-out:</strong> Signing out stops account data from syncing
          to our servers; data already stored locally remains on your device and
          can be cleared by uninstalling the app.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Data deletion:</strong> To request deletion of your account
          and associated data, follow the account deletion steps in Section 8.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>12. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h3>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The current version
        will always be available on this page, with the effective date shown at
        the top. Continued use of the Service after changes constitutes
        acceptance of the updated policy.
      </p>

      <h3>13. Developer and Contact Information</h3>
      <p>
        This policy is provided by and for <strong>Soulful Bhakti</strong>, part
        of <strong>FAMERELAY</strong>. If you have any questions, concerns or
        requests about this Privacy Policy or your data, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:karthik@famerelay.com">karthik@famerelay.com</a>. We
        will respond within a reasonable time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</RootLayout>